rument  more than half of labcorp's pcr testing  is done  on the fda authorized multiplex assay  and that's really important for this  story because  without the spoke pcr testing process  we would not have been able to quickly  and efficiently scale the sequencing  process  to date more than 30 million pcr tests  have been performed across all  methods so even if just over half of  those tests are on the multiplex pcr  assay we have access to really an  unprecedented number of samples for  performing  surveillance activities and this story  wouldn't be complete without  talking about the supply chains  constraints that were  uh needed to that we needed to overcome  the molecular r d group  validated no less than three consumables  or  methods for every step of this process  this includes  plastic plates tips enzymes extraction  reagents collection devices swabs  if you can think of any consumable that  goes into  any test that is performed we have a  backup validated for the backups backup  and this was essential for our success  in pcr testing  because if you run out of even one of  these consumables you  lose the ability to test samples you  can't provide results  you lose customers and ultimately you  then don't have samples  available for sequencing and i'm really  proud to know that  we were one of the few national  diagnostic testing companies to not  exceed more than a three-day average  turnaround time for pcr testing during  the pandemic  and that's because of supply chain  preparedness and because we developed  our own internal  assay to perform pcr testing using  materials that we can source from  multiple other vendors so i just said a  bunch of words about pcr testing and  supply chain  shortage mitigation strategies for  diagnostic testing and i told you that  we were successful  but here's what i said visually the two  animations here track all the positive  pcr samples that we have seen in our  network  since the pandemic began the map on the  left 